WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.975
Appendix A turns all of this
into requests to the provider.

2
00:00:03.975 --> 00:00:08.189
Three habits make a request
hard to deflect: name one item,

3
00:00:08.189 --> 00:00:12.313
cite the basis with a link, and
ask for data, not documents.

4
00:00:12.313 --> 00:00:15.674
The book makes eight requests,
and the slide lists them.

5
00:00:15.674 --> 00:00:20.628
One number shows why trust centers
made the list: when the book checked,

6
00:00:20.628 --> 00:00:24.982
only 110 of 781 Marketplace
listings had a trust-center entry,

7
00:00:24.982 --> 00:00:28.825
and none of the Microsoft
365 government packages did.

8
00:00:28.825 --> 00:00:34.187
Five of the eight requests rest on obligations
the rules already place on providers.

9
00:00:34.187 --> 00:00:38.313
And if the answer is no, a
documented no is evidence too.

10
00:00:38.313 --> 00:00:40.200
Let's close with the decisions.
